   *   - `"pass"`         — lint really ran and was clean. The slice ships, and
   *       the log records that the LOOP certified it, not the agent.
   *   - `"fail"`         — lint really ran and reported problems. The slice
   *       stops, on the truth this time rather than on the paperwork.
   *   - `"inconclusive"` — lint could NOT be run (no `exec` on the handle, a
   *       wedged transport, a timeout, no proof of completion). Nothing was
   *       verified, so the missing certification stands and the slice stops —
   *       the OPPOSITE of `verifyTestRun`'s inconclusive, which ships on the
   *       agent's cert. Deliberate: there the cert existed and was merely
   *       unconfirmed; here there is no cert at all, and an unverifiable
   *       non-cert is no better than the non-cert.
   */
